phy: sprd-ums9632: do without the Type-C extcon for now

ml12 (2026-10-29): usb_add_phy_dev returned -EPROBE_DEFER for good. LK's dtbo gives the PHY extcon = the PMIC's
Type-C block (pmic@1/typec@380, "sprd,ump9651-typec"), which no mainline driver provides (and the UMP9651 MFD is
not ported). Peripheral mode does not need it: the PHY forces VBUS valid. The property goes until there is one.

--- a/drivers/usb/phy/phy-sprd-ums9632.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/phy/phy-sprd-ums9632.c
@@ -313,6 +313,18 @@
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, p);
 
+	/* the Type-C extcon has no driver yet (see above): usb_add_phy_dev would wait for it for ever */
+	{
+		struct property *prop = of_find_property(dev->of_node, "extcon", NULL);
+
+		if (prop) {
+			ret = of_remove_property(dev->of_node, prop);
+			dev_info(dev, "no Type-C extcon driver: extcon dropped (%d)\n", ret);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	dev_info(dev, "usb_add_phy_dev...\n");
 	ret = usb_add_phy_dev(&p->phy);
 	dev_info(dev, "usb_add_phy_dev: %d\n", ret);
